The 101st are starting there enactment of the Tet offensive Vietnam. 

We begin our fight with the battle of Hue which lasted from January 1968 - March 1968. 

North Vietnamese and Viet Cong forces launched a surprise attack and captured much of the city, including the Citadel, leading to weeks of intense urban, house-to-house fighting as U.S. and South Vietnamese troops fought to retake it.

Most of the city was left in ruins, as heavy bombing and artillery was used. 

During their inaugural operation, Cobra Company demonstrated resilience and tactical precision, fighting hard to deliver a highly authentic reenactment of the battle.

